# Delete any scripts that you use once

- If there is a script you make that is only going to be used once, after it has served it's purpose, delete it. 

document-functions: Add docstrings to all new functions and classes

auth-verification: Always verify user authentication and permissions before allowing access to protected resources

delete-one-time-scripts: Delete any scripts that are created for one-time use after they have served their purpose

db-migrations: Run Flask-Migrate commands for any database schema changes and commit the migration files

template-consistency: Ensure both mobile_*.html and desktop templates are updated when making UI changes

error-handling: Add appropriate error handling with flash messages and status codes for all routes

port-management: Always terminate existing processes on port 5006 before starting the development server

session-management: Verify session variables are properly set and cleared during login/logout operations

mobile-testing: Test all features on mobile viewport before committing changes

security-checks: Never store sensitive information like API keys or passwords in version control

clean-imports: Keep import statements organized and remove unused imports

responsive-design: Use responsive design principles for all CSS changes to support various screen sizes

logging-standard: Use app.logger for all logging rather than print statements

api-versioning: Version all API endpoints to maintain backward compatibility

asset-versioning: Add version query parameters to static asset URLs to prevent caching issues

form-validation: Add client-side and server-side validation for all form submissions

config-separation: Keep configuration variables in config.py and environment-specific values in .env files

test-coverage: Write unit tests for all new features and maintain test coverage

accessibility: Ensure all UI elements meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards for accessibility

documentation-updates: Update README.md when adding new features or changing setup requirements
